The [[Ruby Whelp]] is a [[Weapon]] [[Pet]] normally obtained by hatching a [[Ruby Egg]] after two turns spent in the slots of the player's backpack. It deals low-moderate damage, but costs no stamina. At the start of battle, it gains some {{icon/heat}} and reflects some debuffs.

[[Pyromancer]]s have an affinity for the [[Ruby Egg]] and [[Ruby Whelp]] because of [[Dragon Nest]] and the {{icon/heat}} gain, and [[Ranger]]s have an affinity for all [[Pet]]s because of [[Big Bowl of Treats]], so these classes may prioritize the [[Ruby Egg]] slightly more highly.

Every class has their own upgrade on the [[Ruby Whelp]], which is always a larger [[Weapon]] [[Pet]].

[[Mage]]s can combine the [[Ruby Whelp]] with a [[Cupcake]] to craft the [[Cupdrake]], which removes buffs from the opponent and gains buffs on hit.

[[Reaper]]s can combine the [[Ruby Whelp]] with a [[Holo Fire Lizard]] (which requires [[Deck of Cards]]) to craft the [[Ruby Chonk]], which deals higher damage, gains {{icon/heat}} on hit, and stuns once enough {{icon/heat}} is had.

[[Reaper]]s can additionally combine the [[Ruby Whelp]] with a [[White-Eyes Blue Dragon]] (which also requires [[Deck of Cards]]) to craft the [[Ice Dragon]], which deals higher damage, inflicts {{icon/cold}} on hit, and gains loads of {{icon/block}} and reduces {{icon/effect}} damage taken once the opponent reaches enough {{icon/cold}}.

[[Pyromancer]]s can combine the [[Ruby Whelp]] with an [[Draconic Orb]] to craft the [[Obsidian Dragon]], which deals higher damage, and when enough {{icon/heat}} is gained, boosts its damage for the fight and ensures a crit with the [[Weapon]] in front of it.

[[Ranger]]s can combine the [[Ruby Whelp]] with a [[Wisp]] to craft the [[Forest Dragon]], which deals slightly higher base damage, but also gains {{icon/regeneration}} and {{icon/luck}} on hit, and scales off of {{icon/regeneration}}.

[[Berserker]]s can combine the [[Ruby Whelp]] with an [[Essence of Steel]] to craft the [[Panzer Dragon]], which deals slightly higher base damage and additionally, behaves like a larger, more powerful [[Essence of Steel]], which also reflects a bunch of debuffs.

[[Engineer]]s can combine the [[Ruby Whelp]] with a [[Battery]] to craft the [[Thunder Drake]], which deals slightly higher base damage and charges and speeds items in a cone in front of it every few hits.

Finally, [[Adventurer]]s can combine the [[Ruby Whelp]] with a [[Goobert]] using a [[Twine]] to craft the [[Dragon Knight]], which deals slightly higher damage and has some [[Ruby Whelp]]-like properties along with some [[Goobert]] properties, healing on hit, and triggering more often the more items on its sides trigger.
